**RBAC fundamentals:**
- User → has one or more Roles (ADMIN, USER)
- Role → represents a set of permissions
- Endpoint → requires a specific role

**Spring Boot implementation:**
1. UserDetails.getAuthorities() returns roles as GrantedAuthority objects
2. SecurityContext stores these after authentication
3. Authorization checks compare required roles to stored authorities

**Three ways to enforce in Spring:**
```java
// Method 1: HttpSecurity (URL-level)
http.authorizeRequests()
  .antMatchers("/api/admin/**").hasRole("ADMIN")
  .antMatchers("/api/**").hasAnyRole("USER", "ADMIN")
  .anyRequest().authenticated();

// Method 2: @PreAuthorize (method-level)
@PreAuthorize("hasRole('ADMIN')")
public void deleteUser(Long id) { ... }

// Method 3: SecurityContextHolder (programmatic)
Authentication auth = SecurityContextHolder.getContext().getAuthentication();
boolean isAdmin = auth.getAuthorities().stream()
  .anyMatch(a -> a.getAuthority().equals("ROLE_ADMIN"));
```
